WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.500
Look at a face upside down and something strange can happen.
Turn it upright and the parts suddenly seem wrong.

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:13.000
Peter Thompson documented the Thatcher illusion in 1980.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:19.500
But here's the interesting correction: later studies found
similar orientation effects with non-face objects.

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:26.500
So a startling effect is real—but the first explanation
may be too simple.

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:34.000
That matters when an audio product promises extraordinary
results. Read the evidence, try a free twelve-minute routine,

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:42.000
and ask what the product itself has actually been shown to do.
